  "title": "Update Fraud Flags by Risk Score",
  "prompt": "You are managing a fintech app's transaction approvals table. Each transaction has a risk_score (integer 0\u2013100) and a fraud_flag (boolean). Business rules require: (1) any transaction with risk_score \u2265 80 must have fraud_flag set to TRUE; (2) any transaction with risk_score < 50 must have fraud_flag set to FALSE; (3) transactions with risk_score between 50 and 79 (inclusive) should keep their current fraud_flag unchanged. Write a single UPDATE statement that applies these rules to all rows in the approvals table. Then write a SELECT statement that returns all columns from approvals, ordered by transaction_id ascending, to confirm the final state.",
  "schema_ddl": "CREATE TABLE approvals (transaction_id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY, merchant_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL, amount DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL, risk_score INT NOT NULL CHECK (risk_score BETWEEN 0 AND 100), fraud_flag BOOLEAN NOT NULL, processed_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL);",
